    "reason": "Semantics and structure confirmed (71/94 opcodes; target 221 vs candidate 228 bytes): mem_Lock the source mask, compute size via ((( width*4+31)/32)*height+3)*4 on Tandy (displayType==10) or width*height/2+12 otherwise, mem_Alloc(size,1,\"tdyballoon\") [the 'tdyballoon' debug tag was recovered directly from the DGROUP literal pool in assets/SIMANTW.EXE at both original operand offsets 0x1d3d and 0x1d48, both resolving to the same 11-byte NUL-terminated string], mem_Lock the new object, write width/height/type=3 unconditionally then flag=0x84 or 4 via a SECOND independent displayType test, call MaskMono2Tandy(newObj+8, srcObj+8), unlock both handles, free the source handle, return the new handle. Two residual mismatches survive four source-shape attempts (explicit width/height locals, register hints, CSE via direct src-> access, inlining the size expression into the mem_Alloc call): (1) 'height' (the second struct field read, es:[bx+0xa]) never gets a register home matching target's DI -- every attempt spills it to a stack temp (bp-2) that's reloaded twice, while target keeps it live in DI across the mem_Alloc call and both branches; (2) the string literal \"tdyballoon\" compiles as a fresh isolated-TU literal-pool contribution rather than reusing the two original historical addresses (0x1d3d and 0x1d48, NOT deduplicated in the original binary even though byte-identical), so its selector/DATA fixup never lines up. Best candidate: build/grind/agentH/_ConvertMonoMaskToTandy.c.",
